  "difficulty_level": "H2",
  "difficulty_reason": "Supplying the named Patterson--Sullivan existence, Busemann-cocycle continuity, relative Ancona and quasi-conformality prerequisites leaves a source-local partial-shadow estimate in the twisted transition-point setting: the lower bound is reduced to positive measure of a loxodromic inverse shadow combined with equivariance and the coarse Busemann cocycle, while the upper bound combines relative Ancona multiplicativity along transition points with the conical Radon--Nikodym derivative and constants uniform in r and in the group element. The mechanism is not the classical Sullivan shadow lemma: the shadows are cut out by (eta,L)-transition points, the constants must be uniform in the group element, and the authors record that the upper bound for the usual shadow remains unknown. Adapting the argument of [Yan22, Lemmas 4.1 and 4.2] to these Green-function-twisted PS measures, with Lemma 4.6 replacing Lemma 2.19 there, is above ordinary qualification hyperbolic geometry and probability.",
